From 83a4e2b7a0000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 2ax4 <2ax4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play the glass home button without the ownership check

The offline accounts patch reduced play_press to (prepared, busy), but the
glass home's play group still passed self.owner (Option<bool>) to it, so
the binary and its tests could not compile at all (E0061). This call site
appeared in upstream 0.2.39 and was never covered by the patch set; it is
what kept every offline release assetless since 0.2.38.
---
 launcher/src/glass_home.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/launcher/src/glass_home.rs b/launcher/src/glass_home.rs
index 6e018f2fe..83a4e2b7a 100644
--- a/launcher/src/glass_home.rs
+++ b/launcher/src/glass_home.rs
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ impl Launcher {
                     Some(_) => (tr("Update"), "download-04"),
                     None => (tr("Play"), "play"),
                 };
-                let press = play_press(ready, self.owner, false);
+                let press = play_press(ready, false);
                 let main = body(label.into(), icon).id("play").cursor_pointer();
                 let main = match (&update, press) {
                     (Some(_), _) => main.on_click(cx.listener(|this, _: &ClickEvent, _, cx| {
